    "top_frame": "Shutdown early. The bats never showed up.",
    "what_this_means": "Texas silenced the Yankees for three innings straight, and once Rodriguez surrendered two in the fourth, any path back disappeared. Eight strikeouts in five hits is not an offensive line that competes in May. The division doesn't wait for lineups to find themselves. Every team in this race is built to punish dead swings and empty at-bats. Rice went 3-for-4 and it didn't matter because he was one voice in a silent room. This is how stretches start.",
    "what_to_watch": "The concern isn't that they lost a day game on the road. It's that they looked flat doing it. One win in the last two games, eight strikeouts at a ballpark where contact matters more than power. This isn't a variance problem yet, but it's the edge of one. Balanced offense doesn't survive when half the lineup goes quiet and the pitcher can't extend past four innings. The formula only holds when both sides click. They stopped today.",
